categories          java devel
# The SDK is Apache-2. The bundled dependencies are Apache-2, BSD (api-common,
# google-auth-library, protobuf-java), MIT (slf4j-api) and public domain (json).
license             Apache-2 BSD MIT public-domain
supported_archs     noarch
platforms           {darwin any}
maintainers         nomaintainer

description         Databricks SDK for Java, with its runtime dependencies

long_description    The Databricks SDK for Java covers all public Databricks \
                    REST API operations and provides unified authentication \
                    (OAuth, personal access tokens and other Databricks \
                    credential providers). This port installs the SDK as a \
                    self-contained package: the SDK jar together with the \
                    exact versions of its runtime dependencies that this SDK \
                    release resolves to (Jackson, Guava, Google Auth, Apache \
                    HttpClient, Apache Commons, protobuf-java, SLF4J and \
                    others), in a private directory, plus a classpath file \
                    that lists them all. The SDK can then be used without \
                    Maven or Gradle, from java -cp, jshell or scripts.

homepage            https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/sdk-java.html

java.version        8+
java.fallback       openjdk11

